package unit

// workedExamples are qualitative BTD6 progression examples shown to the planner.
// Transcribed from the retired BTD6-UNIT-EXAMPLES.md (see docs/BTD6-REFERENCE.md);
// they teach progression, not contracts.
const workedExamplesJSON = "[{\"name\":\"Dart Monkey top path\",\"base\":\"One cheap short range dart with limited pierce.\",\"milestones\":{\"tier1\":\"Sharp Shots: more targets pierced by the same dart.\",\"tier2\":\"Razor Sharp Shots: more pierce again.\",\"tier3\":\"Spike-o-pult: replace darts with slower spiked balls that rebound from obstacles, with greater damage, range and pierce.\",\"tier4\":\"Juggernaut: develop those balls with more pierce, faster delivery, Lead access and Ceramic/Fortified bonuses plus brief knockback.\",\"tier5\":\"Ultra-Juggernaut: a stronger parent ball splits into smaller Juggernaut balls, retaining useful wall interactions.\"},\"buyFor\":\"Dense groups along favorable wall corridors.\",\"capstoneValue\":\"Branching balls extend the established corridor clearing role.\",\"crosspaths\":\"Middle improves firing frequency. Bottom adds reach and personal Camo detection.\",\"limitations\":\"Open maps reduce rebound value. Walls, rebound timing, child inheritance and enemy bonuses need explicit engine support; a generic area hit does not implement them.\"},{\"name\":\"Dart Monkey bottom path\",\"base\":\"The same ordinary dart attacker.\",\"milestones\":{\"tier1\":\"Long Range Darts: extend reach and projectile lifetime.\",\"tier2\":\"Enhanced Eyesight: improve reach and delivery, add personal Camo detection and prioritization.\",\"tier3\":\"Crossbow: replace the dart with a stronger, longer range crossbow shot.\",\"tier4\":\"Sharp Shooter: improve damage and rate, add a critical shot after a repeating shot count.\",\"tier5\":\"Crossbow Master: improve rate, reach, pierce and damage, make critical shots more frequent and broaden resistant target coverage.\"},\"buyFor\":\"Long range precision with personal detection.\",\"capstoneValue\":\"Much stronger sustained crossbow performance; no unrelated subsystem is necessary.\",\"crosspaths\":\"Top adds pierce. Middle accelerates shots and therefore recurring critical shots over time.\",\"limitations\":\"Critical shots are automatic and count based, not manual or random. Engine support for counters and resistance coverage must be checked.\"},{\"name\":\"Boomerang Monkey middle path\",\"base\":\"A curved boomerang attack that can hit several bloons.\",\"milestones\":{\"tier1\":\"Faster Throwing: increase firing frequency.\",\"tier2\":\"Faster Rangs: increase frequency and projectile travel speed.\",\"tier3\":\"Bionic Boomerang: greatly increase ordinary frequency and add a MOAB damage bonus.\",\"tier4\":\"Turbo Charge: manually boost the existing attack speed and damage for a temporary window.\",\"tier5\":\"Perma Charge: make extreme speed permanent, improve baseline damage, and retain the ability as a further temporary damage increase.\"},\"buyFor\":\"Sustained attack throughput with a controllable burst window.\",\"capstoneValue\":\"A stronger permanent state and a useful evolved active, rather than a new weapon.\",\"crosspaths\":\"Top adds pierce for groups. Bottom adds damage and Lead access.\",\"limitations\":\"Usually needs external Camo support. Firing frequency and travel speed are distinct. MOAB bonuses and Lead permissions are not generic damage.\"}]"

// progressionReference is retained BTD6 progression context for planning and design guidance.
const progressionReference = "Retained BTD6 progression examples: community wiki upgrade rows accessed 2026-09-20, not a pinned game-build audit or current balance certification. Prices below are incremental Medium purchases. Retained overview, total-cost, crosspath and version-history sections sometimes disagree; use the identified upgrade rows as historical examples, not universal multipliers or a required price curve.\nDart bottom path: T3 Crossbow costs 575, deals 3 damage and reaches 60 range. T4 Sharp Shooter costs 2050, deals 6 ordinary damage, changes the interval from 0.95s to 0.475s, and adds a 50-damage critical every 10 shots. T5 Crossbow Master costs 21500, deals 8 ordinary damage, attacks every 0.2375s, raises pierce from 4 to 8 and range from 60 to 80, and delivers an 80-damage critical every 5 shots. The retained row also grants all-type damage access. T4 buys a stronger precision weapon and recurring spikes; T5 buys much faster sustained fire, more frequent spikes, reach and group capacity together. Its high incremental price does not imply that it always beats several cheaper towers.\nDart tradeoff: 2-0-5 benefits from extra pierce when a straight lane supplies enough targets; 0-2-5 fires faster and reaches its shot-count critical sooner in elapsed time. Extra pierce is unused against one isolated target, while multiple cheap placements need space and useful firing coverage. Critical counters, projectile travel and per-type damage permissions are unsupported analogies here unless the supplied Definition explicitly implements them; ordinary damage is not a critical-hit system.\nBoomerang middle path: T3 Bionic Boomerang costs 1250, fires 8x faster than the ordinary base tower and adds 1 damage to MOAB-class targets. T4 Turbo Charge costs 4200 and temporarily fires 5x faster with 1 extra damage for 10s on a 45s cooldown. T5 Perma Charge costs 35000, makes the former Turbo speed permanent, deals 4 ordinary damage, and retains an active adding 8 damage for 15s. This retained effect row does not specify the T5 cooldown; do not invent it. T4 buys a timed answer to a dangerous push; T5 buys a much stronger permanent firing state plus a further burst, rather than merely extending one stat by a universal ratio.\nBoomerang tradeoff: 2-4-0 adds pierce for dense groups; 0-4-2 adds damage and Lead access for tougher targets but can leave weaker cleanup after blimps break apart. A timed burst needs threats inside range during activation, and most builds still need Camo support. Enemy-class damage bonuses, Lead exceptions and curved or returning trajectories remain unsupported analogies; the Definition may support an ordinary attack boost without reproducing these other effects.\nSources: research/btd6/source-snapshots/btd6-dart-2026-09-20.txt, upgrade rows at lines 79, 85 and 91, https://bloons.fandom.com/wiki/Dart_Monkey_(BTD6); research/btd6/source-snapshots/btd6-dart-crosspaths-2026-09-20.txt, Crossbow Master discussion at lines 115-124, https://bloons.fandom.com/wiki/Crosspathing/Dart_Monkey. Boomerang: research/btd6/source-snapshots/btd6-boomerang-2026-09-20.txt, upgrade rows at lines 48, 54 and 60, https://bloons.fandom.com/wiki/Boomerang_Monkey_(BTD6); research/btd6/source-snapshots/btd6-boomerang-crosspaths-2026-09-20.txt, Turbo Charge discussion at lines 90-93, https://bloons.fandom.com/wiki/Crosspathing/Boomerang_Monkey."
